  EUD-227, task 15 addendum to task 13's fixture set (see fixtures/tsl/README.md and
  tasks.md task 13 Notes addendum for the full rationale).

  Task 13's lotl-valid.xml only ever points at tl-national-a-valid.xml and
  tl-national-b-valid.xml, both granted-only and both valid — it cannot exercise AC-02
  ("one national list tampered, the LOTL and the other lists are fine, sync continues"),
  AC-03 through the real DSS pipeline (a valid list with three services in three different
  statuses), or EC-01 (an unreachable national list) end to end, because no fixture LOTL
  references tl-national-tampered.xml, tl-national-three-statuses.xml, or an unreachable
  location. This LOTL variant, added by task 15, points at a mix of:
    - tl-national-b-valid.xml (BB, granted)              -> AC-01/AC-02 "other lists are fine"
    - tl-national-tampered.xml (ZZ, signature broken)     -> AC-02 / ES-02(list-level)
    - tl-national-three-statuses.xml (CC, three statuses) -> AC-03 through a real sync
    - a location whose hostname is never registered as a network alias in the container
      test -> EC-01 (deterministic DNS failure, not a stopped-container timing race)
